What are Semiconductor Materials?
Semiconductor materials form the foundation of modern electronics, enabling the fabrication and packaging of all electronic devices. These specialized materials fall into two key categories: wafer fabrication materials (silicon wafers, photomasks, photoresists, wet chemicals, gases) and packaging materials (IC substrates, lead frames, bonding wires). As chip designs become more advanced and applications more demanding, the requirements for these materials grow increasingly stringent, creating both opportunities and challenges across the supply chain.
